  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "QSI",
          "fullName": "QSI — Quantum Security Intelligence",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/AlekseyKoks-in/quantumwebhunter",
          "version": "1.2.0",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "DEP-KNOWN-ADVISORY",
              "name": "DepKnownAdvisory",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "block-buffer 0.10.4 is affected by GHSA-qwgh-2vcv-g2f7"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "dependencies",
                  "known_vulnerable_component"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.0"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OSV.dev reports GHSA-qwgh-2vcv-g2f7 for crates.io package block-buffer at version 0.10.4: block_buffer: panic corrupts inline buffer position. The advisory names no affected functions, so reachability was not determined. Upgrade to a fixed version (none published yet; see the advisory for mitigations). Advisory data comes from OSV.dev at the recorded time. Reachability is judged from names, not a call graph: the affected functions the advisory lists against the identifiers in the audited product code, a Cargo feature it says is off by default against the audited manifests, the platforms it lists against the declared Rust targets. Indirect calls (traits, macros, other dependencies) are not followed."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "OSV.dev reports GHSA-qwgh-2vcv-g2f7 for crates.io package block-buffer at version 0.10.4: block_buffer: panic corrupts inline buffer position. The advisory names no affected functions, so reachability was not determined. Upgrade to a fixed version (none published yet; see the advisory for mitigations). Advisory data comes from OSV.dev at the recorded time. Reachability is judged from names, not a call graph: the affected functions the advisory lists against the identifiers in the audited product code, a Cargo feature it says is off by default against the audited manifests, the platforms it lists against the declared Rust targets. Indirect calls (traits, macros, other dependencies) are not followed."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-qwgh-2vcv-g2f7"
            },
            {
              "id": "KEY-QV-PUBLIC",
              "name": "KeyQvPublic",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Quantum-vulnerable RSA key (2048-bit) in responsible_disclosure.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "post_quantum",
                  "pq_long_term_risk"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.0"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A RSA 2048-bit public key was found (line 11). Inventory and plan migration to ML-DSA (FIPS 204) or SLH-DSA (FIPS 205), in a hybrid/composite form where the ecosystem supports it.. This is a forward-looking risk that depends on the arrival of a cryptographically relevant quantum computer (CRQC). No such computer is publicly known to exist today; the timeline is uncertain. It is not a present-day exploitable vulnerability."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A RSA 2048-bit public key was found (line 11). Inventory and plan migration to ML-DSA (FIPS 204) or SLH-DSA (FIPS 205), in a hybrid/composite form where the ecosystem supports it.. This is a forward-looking risk that depends on the arrival of a cryptographically relevant quantum computer (CRQC). No such computer is publicly known to exist today; the timeline is uncertain. It is not a present-day exploitable vulnerability."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://doi.org/10.1137/S0097539795293172"
            },
            {
              "id": "DEP-ADVISORY-UNRATED",
              "name": "DepAdvisoryUnrated",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "crypto-bigint 0.5.5 is affected by RUSTSEC-2026-0387 (no severity rating)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "dependencies",
                  "known_vulnerable_component"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.0"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OSV.dev reports RUSTSEC-2026-0387 for crates.io package crypto-bigint at version 0.5.5: Multiple timing variability issues in operations intended to be constant-time. The advisory carries neither a CVSS vector nor a database severity, so QSI rates it low and preliminary until it is triaged. The advisory names no affected functions, so reachability was not determined. Triage the advisory; upgrade to a fixed version (0.7.6) if it applies. Advisory data comes from OSV.dev at the recorded time. The advisory has no severity rating. Reachability is judged from names, not a call graph: the affected functions the advisory lists against the identifiers in the audited product code, a Cargo feature it says is off by default against the audited manifests, the platforms it lists against the declared Rust targets. Indirect calls (traits, macros, other dependencies) are not followed."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "OSV.dev reports RUSTSEC-2026-0387 for crates.io package crypto-bigint at version 0.5.5: Multiple timing variability issues in operations intended to be constant-time. The advisory carries neither a CVSS vector nor a database severity, so QSI rates it low and preliminary until it is triaged. The advisory names no affected functions, so reachability was not determined. Triage the advisory; upgrade to a fixed version (0.7.6) if it applies. Advisory data comes from OSV.dev at the recorded time. The advisory has no severity rating. Reachability is judged from names, not a call graph: the affected functions the advisory lists against the identifiers in the audited product code, a Cargo feature it says is off by default against the audited manifests, the platforms it lists against the declared Rust targets. Indirect calls (traits, macros, other dependencies) are not followed."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://osv.dev/vulnerability/RUSTSEC-2026-0387"
            },
            {
              "id": "DEP-NO-PQC-LIBRARY",
              "name": "DepNoPqcLibrary",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No post-quantum capable cryptographic library detected"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "post_quantum",
                  "insufficient_data"
                ],
                "security-severity": "1.0"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Across 3 dependency manifests, QSI found crypto libraries (curve25519-dalek, ecdsa, ed25519-dalek, p256, p384, ring, rsa, rustls, secp256k1, x25519-dalek) but none from its PQC-capable list. Confirm where PQC support will come from (TLS terminator, KMS/HSM, library upgrade). Absence of evidence is not evidence of absence: system libraries and transitive dependencies may not be listed."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Across 3 dependency manifests, QSI found crypto libraries (curve25519-dalek, ecdsa, ed25519-dalek, p256, p384, ring, rsa, rustls, secp256k1, x25519-dalek) but none from its PQC-capable list. Confirm where PQC support will come from (TLS terminator, KMS/HSM, library upgrade). Absence of evidence is not evidence of absence: system libraries and transitive dependencies may not be listed."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final"
            },
            {
              "id": "DEP-ADVISORY-INFORMATIONAL",
              "name": "DepAdvisoryInformational",
              "shortDescription": {
